# grav_tether addon - Weapons hold-click popup for the sbs_utils grav_tether primitive.
#
# The physics + impulse enforcement live in sbs_utils.procedural.grav_tether (the
# primitive auto-runs its own tick, so just loading this addon + calling attach is
# enough - no activation step). This file is only the UX: a Weapons HOLD-CLICK on an
# object raises a hold-menu whose action is chosen by the target's ROLE.
#
# Engine-verified: the hold-click popup shows and toggles tether state in real Cosmos.
#
# Role -> mode (confirmed roles; pickups carry item,upgrade):
#   item / upgrade                     -> Reel (draw in for collection)
#   lm_tether_haulable (LM_TETHER_HAULABLE:
#     station / asteroid / __npc__ /
#     derelict / wreck / hulk)         -> Tow (rope 500, stiffness ~5) or Lock (rigid)
#   black_hole in reach                -> Slingshot (swing, rope clamped clear of the well)
#   anything else                      -> nothing
#   already tethered                   -> Release
#
# AN ALLOWLIST, NOT A BLACKLIST. This used to read "anything that is not a pickup, a
# station, a rock or an NPC gets a rigid Grav Lock", which meant a gunner could Grav Lock
# a BLACK HOLE. That makes the hole the LOAD: the beam reels it onto the hull, the
# library caps the ship to impulse so it cannot warp away, and black_hole_lethal_watch
# (collisions/collision.mast) explodes anything within 500u of it - then the hole stays
# parked wherever it was dropped, killing whatever comes near for the rest of the match.
# The same branch also offered a rigid lock on every nebula, mine, planet, marker and GM
# camera rig. The library now refuses to PULL an anchor at all (grav_tether ANCHOR_ROLES);
# this menu is the other half - it stops offering it.
#
# Impulse-only is canonical (old-game Arena a28): the primitive caps the source back to
# impulse by default (grav_tether_set_overspeed_default to change to snap/off).

# THE OBJECT UNDER THE CURSOR, NOT THE WEAPONS LOCK. `WEAPONS_POPUP_ID` is what the
# gunner actually held the button on; `WEAPONS_SELECTED_ID` is whatever the console
# happens to have targeted, which for a tether is the wrong object nearly every time -
# you tow the derelict while you are still locked on the raider shooting at you. Gated on
# the selection, this menu offered to tether the WEAPONS TARGET no matter what was
# clicked, and offered nothing at all when the console had no lock. It is 0 for a
# hold-click on empty space, so the guard is required, not defensive.
# Nothing is on offer mid-slingshot. The arc is a few seconds long and the helm is
# commandeered for the duration; letting go half way round would drop the ship on an
# arbitrary bearing, which is not an abort anyone wants.
//popup/weapons if has_any_role(WEAPONS_ORIGIN_ID, "__player__") and WEAPONS_POPUP_ID != 0 and WEAPONS_POPUP_ID != WEAPONS_ORIGIN_ID and not lm_tether_sling_is(WEAPONS_ORIGIN_ID)
    # grav_tether_BETWEEN (the registry, either way round), not grav_tether_get (the live
    # engine connection) and not grav_tether_has (directional). Two ways this goes wrong,
    # and both end the same: the menu re-offers the grab and never offers Release, so a
    # crew cannot let go.
    #   * `get` reads None for most of a perfectly normal tow, because a Tow is a rope
    #     TOGGLE - it drops the connection whenever the load is inside the rope length.
    #   * `has` is directional, and a SWING is registered the other way up: the anchor is
    #     the source and the ship is the load. So has(me, that) is False for the very
    #     slingshot this menu just opened.
    gt_has = grav_tether_between(WEAPONS_ORIGIN_ID, WEAPONS_POPUP_ID)
    if gt_has:
        + "Release":
            grav_tether_release_between(WEAPONS_ORIGIN_ID, WEAPONS_POPUP_ID)
    if not gt_has and has_any_role(WEAPONS_POPUP_ID, "item,upgrade"):
        + "Grav Reel":
            grav_tether_reel(WEAPONS_ORIGIN_ID, WEAPONS_POPUP_ID)
    # Tow AND Lock on the same set: dragging a derelict behind you and grabbing it
    # rigidly are both reasonable and only the gunner knows which is wanted - it is the
    # same pair of verbs the fighter popup below already offers.
    if not gt_has and lm_tether_haulable(WEAPONS_POPUP_ID):
        + "Grav Tow":
            grav_tether_tow(WEAPONS_ORIGIN_ID, WEAPONS_POPUP_ID, 500)
        + "Grav Lock":
            grav_tether_lock(WEAPONS_ORIGIN_ID, WEAPONS_POPUP_ID)
    # A hole is an ANCHOR, never a load. A slingshot is the one thing a tether may do with
    # one - and it is not a tether at all underneath: an invisible carrier flies the arc
    # and the engine holds the ship welded to it, so the curve is engine motion rather
    # than something re-pointed ten times a second. See lm_tether_slingshot_hole.
    #
    # WIDE is clamped clear of the gravity well. CLOSE is inside it: faster, because the
    # arc is shorter, and the hole's own pull is fighting the carrier the whole way.
    if not gt_has and lm_tether_hole_in_reach(WEAPONS_ORIGIN_ID, WEAPONS_POPUP_ID) and lm_tether_sling_ready(WEAPONS_ORIGIN_ID):
        + "Slingshot (wide)":
            lm_tether_slingshot_hole(WEAPONS_ORIGIN_ID, WEAPONS_POPUP_ID)
        + "Slingshot (close)":
            lmgt_tight = lm_tether_hole_close_rope(WEAPONS_POPUP_ID)
            lm_tether_slingshot_hole(WEAPONS_ORIGIN_ID, WEAPONS_POPUP_ID, lmgt_tight)


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# FIGHTER: the nose is the cursor.
#
# A pilot gets one button (the cockpit console owns it; see hangar/hangar.mast). It
# nose-aims, and when the target says what to do it just does it - a rock is an anchor, a
# pod is a pickup, and making a pilot confirm that is a menu for the sake of a menu. When
# the target is genuinely a CHOICE the button synthesizes this popup on it instead.
#
# Path B: the event is fabricated, not clicked, so this consumes NO select channel -
# comms, weapons and science selects all stay free. Capital ships reach the same actions
# through //popup/weapons above; this is the same verbs, a different way in.

//popup/tether if has_any_role(TETHER_ORIGIN_ID, "__player__,cockpit")
    lmtf_towed = grav_tether_involves(TETHER_ORIGIN_ID)
    << "Grav-tether: {lm_tether_target_name(TETHER_SELECTED_ID)}"

    if lmtf_towed:
        + "Release":
            grav_tether_release_any(TETHER_ORIGIN_ID)
            lm_tether_cycle_reset(TETHER_ORIGIN_ID)

    if not lmtf_towed:
        + "Tow":
            lm_tether_apply(TETHER_ORIGIN_ID, TETHER_SELECTED_ID, "tow")
        + "Lock":
            lm_tether_apply(TETHER_ORIGIN_ID, TETHER_SELECTED_ID, "lock")
        + "Swing":
            lm_tether_apply(TETHER_ORIGIN_ID, TETHER_SELECTED_ID, "swing")
        # Target correction from INSIDE the popup - still no select channel. Walks
        # outward through the cone and wraps, so it can never dead-end.
        + "Cycle target":
            lmtf_next = lm_tether_cycle_next(TETHER_ORIGIN_ID)
            if lmtf_next is not None:
                lm_tether_open_popup(TETHER_ORIGIN_ID, lmtf_next.id)


# The beam breaks under hard fire, so towing under attack is a real risk rather than a
# free ride. //damage/object fires per hit and carries the amount in EVENT.sub_float;
# only a heavy hit shakes a tether loose, or every skirmish would drop every load.
//damage/object if grav_tether_involves(DAMAGE_TARGET_ID) or grav_tether_involves(DAMAGE_ORIGIN_ID)
    # Declared in __init__.mast; defaulted again here so a shot arriving before this
    # addon's top level has run cannot NameError the route out of existence.
    default LM_TETHER_BREAK_DAMAGE = 15
    lmgt_hit = EVENT.sub_float or 0
    ->END if lmgt_hit < LM_TETHER_BREAK_DAMAGE
    if grav_tether_involves(DAMAGE_TARGET_ID):
        # Tell whoever was HAULING, not whatever was hit. Two reasons the old
        # comms_broadcast(DAMAGE_TARGET_ID, ...) was wrong, and the second one raised:
        #   * the shot object is usually the LOAD, and a barge is not a player ship - it
        #     has no waterfall to write to. The haulers are its tether SOURCES. (When the
        #     towing ship itself is shot it is a source, so it tells itself.)
        #   * the same hit can DESTROY what it shook loose, and comms_broadcast to a freed
        #     object raises "invalid space object while calling SendMessageToPlayerShip".
        #     A failing expression stops the command, so the route ended there - once per
        #     qualifying hit, for the rest of the mission.
        # Gather before releasing: grav_tether_release_any drops the very association
        # these lookups read.
        lmgt_told = grav_tether_sources_of(DAMAGE_TARGET_ID)
        if grav_tether_targets_of(DAMAGE_TARGET_ID):
            lmgt_told = lmgt_told + [DAMAGE_TARGET_ID]
        lmgt_told = [lmgt_t for lmgt_t in lmgt_told if object_exists(lmgt_t)]
        grav_tether_release_any(DAMAGE_TARGET_ID)
        if lmgt_told:
            comms_broadcast(lmgt_told, "Grav-tether shaken loose by the hit.")


# Ran the reserves dry mid-haul. The library drops the load rather than pinning the ship
# at zero energy - being slow is a mechanic, being stranded is not.
//shared/signal/grav_tether_dry
    default SOURCE_ID = 0
    ->END if SOURCE_ID == 0
    comms_broadcast(SOURCE_ID, "Grav-tether offline - not enough power to hold the load.")


# The haul changed weight class, or a hull joined it. Every cost this beam charges used
# to be invisible: a crew towing a starbase was capped to impulse, cut to a quarter
# throttle and burning its reserves, and the ship simply felt broken. The only two signals
# that existed both fired after the haul had already failed.
#
# Addressed to SOURCE_ID, not the load. The library emits one of these PER SHIP on the
# beam - which is what a per-console readout wants - so broadcasting to the target would
# print four identical lines into one waterfall the moment a fourth tug joined.
//shared/signal/grav_tether_strain
    default SOURCE_ID = 0
    default STRAIN = ""
    default PULLERS = 1
    ->END if SOURCE_ID == 0
    if PULLERS > 1:
        comms_broadcast(SOURCE_ID, f"Grav-tether: {PULLERS} hulls on the beam - load is {STRAIN}.")
    if PULLERS <= 1 and STRAIN == "overloaded":
        comms_broadcast(SOURCE_ID, "Grav-tether overloaded - this needs another ship on it.")
    if PULLERS <= 1 and STRAIN != "overloaded":
        comms_broadcast(SOURCE_ID, f"Grav-tether under {STRAIN} load - engines are paying for it.")


# Too fast to get hold of. Says WHY, or the button just looks broken.
//shared/signal/grav_tether_too_fast
    default SOURCE_ID = 0
    ->END if SOURCE_ID == 0
    comms_broadcast(SOURCE_ID, "Target is under power - cripple its engines before you can get a lock.")


# A hulk cashed in at a friendly station. The tick does the work; this is the telling.
//shared/signal/lm_tether_salvage_delivered
    default SHIP_ID = 0
    default UNITS = 0
    ->END if SHIP_ID == 0
    comms_broadcast(SHIP_ID, f"Hulk delivered - {UNITS} units of salvage aboard.")


# --- phase 5 -------------------------------------------------------------------------
# A black hole is the anchor the swing was invented for. Offered only when one is
# actually in reach and the throw has recharged; the arc is clamped clear of the gravity
# well - the tether must never be the thing that drops someone in.
//popup/tether if has_any_role(TETHER_ORIGIN_ID, "__player__,cockpit") and lm_tether_nearest_hole(TETHER_ORIGIN_ID) is not None and lm_tether_sling_ready(TETHER_ORIGIN_ID)
    + "Slingshot the black hole":
        lm_tether_slingshot_hole(TETHER_ORIGIN_ID, lm_tether_nearest_hole(TETHER_ORIGIN_ID))


# Pinned by a hostile beam. Says what to do about it, because a ship that is suddenly
# not going anywhere with no explanation reads as a bug.
//shared/signal/lm_tether_pinned
    default SHIP_ID = 0
    ->END if SHIP_ID == 0
    comms_broadcast(SHIP_ID, "Caught in a hostile grav-tether - burn hard away to tear loose.")

//shared/signal/lm_tether_broke_free
    default SHIP_ID = 0
    ->END if SHIP_ID == 0
    comms_broadcast(SHIP_ID, "Tether snapped - you are free.")


# Thrown. Says which pass it was, because the crew chose.
//shared/signal/lm_tether_sling_start
    default SHIP_ID = 0
    default CLOSE = False
    ->END if SHIP_ID == 0
    if CLOSE:
        comms_broadcast(SHIP_ID, "Slingshot - close pass. Hold on.")
    if not CLOSE:
        comms_broadcast(SHIP_ID, "Slingshot - coming round the far side.")


# Out the other side. A close pass costs a system, so say so rather than let the crew
# find the damage on the grid and wonder what hit them.
//shared/signal/lm_tether_sling_done
    default SHIP_ID = 0
    default CLOSE = False
    ->END if SHIP_ID == 0
    if CLOSE:
        comms_broadcast(SHIP_ID, "Clear of the well - that pass strained a system.")
    if not CLOSE:
        comms_broadcast(SHIP_ID, "Clear of the well. Helm is yours.")


# The cooldown timer emits this itself (set_timer signal=), so nothing has to poll it.
//shared/signal/lm_tether_sling_ready
    default TIMER_AGENT_ID = 0
    ->END if TIMER_AGENT_ID == 0
    comms_broadcast(TIMER_AGENT_ID, "Slingshot recharged.")
